  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Michael King carried them through six. Jackson Merrill supplied the only runs that mattered.",
    "what_this_means": "King let Houston scatter three hits and one run across six innings, then handed the lead to a bullpen that did not let it slip. Merrill's two-run homer in the first inning became the complete offensive story. Two runs on five hits is barely a pulse, but it was enough. Estrada struck out two in the eighth. Morejon held another inning clean. Mason Miller closed it out without drama. This is a team that wins 3\u20132 games the way other teams win 6\u20132 games. With pitching that holds and offense that doesn't waste what it gets. The margin is always thin. The formula works when it works.",
